                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I know, I know.. you all love my long reviews, thorough, written in an awesome English..\nNo, just kidding, I'm hitting 300 and it's a great milestone, trying just for free to help other players :)\nI know my English sucks and I'm not good at writing, but I'm always trying to do my best.\nSanta Run has for sure an awesome word in its title, and it's basically telling you what you've got to do with it - run away, don't even think about buying this game or getting it for free or even getting it in a random bundle like I did some weeks ago.\nThis game is really one of the worst things I ever saw on the Internet since the '90s.\nBut I'm an historian and I always have to honour my degrees, my working fields, my passions..\nOk guys let's get it straight to the point - this thing is an unplayable pile of crap, made in ten minutes and fully and completely playable in the same leap of time.\nI'm not sure about the word \"leap\" here since with Gau in Final Fantasy VI has another meaning but it's very similar to the Italian one so let's just pretend that they're from the same Latin or Greek root.\nBeing a Russian game, on opening it you can choose between English or Russian but you'll find only four words in the whole game so I think you probably can beat this also in some kind of spoken tribal language.\nThe settings are there only for two purposes: on one hand they make you choose between full screen and windowed mode, and on the other hand they are going to tell you which will be your forced keys - yeah, you can't customize anything.\nAnd for the sake of this review, they're W and S - with W you'll move Santa up, with S down. Esc for the menu. Nothing else.\nClicking on play will let you choose between two settings - city or forest. It's basically the same crap, some Paint-drawn trees, gifts, buildings, streets and enemies.\nYour character will move up and down in a diagonal way even if you don't touch anything - he will move with the same speed, but you can choose up or down or simply let him go on his own way. Your only objective is to collect gift scattered on the ground, for which there is a huge counter in the upper right side of the screen. \nCity and forest will feature two different kind of enemies, like, dogs, or witches (?), everything's drawn so so badly that one can't even say if he's avoiding a woman or a deer.\nThere are no health points or such, so on hitting an enemy you'll automatically start at the beginning of the level. And the two levels not only are the same - just some color changes - but they're also endless. Basically, without purpose or difficulty progression, you'll go on forever collecting gift boxes and avoiding enemies, everything moving slowly and with a background music that gets annoying after two minutes being a standard MIDI Christmas-like thing.\nOverall, this is really something you've got to avoid at all costs. There's no purpose, there's no gameplay. You just play as Santa, going up and down, collecting boxes automatically and avoiding enemies while everything will move extremely slow and so you could go on endlessly, if only there was some kind of meaning. But there are no bosses, no changes in the scenario, nothing, really. \nYou can't kill enemies, you can't do anything. Just stroll up and down and avoid things. And collect gifts.\nSo.. there's nothing really more to add. After five minutes, you'll have already seen everything that this game has to offer. The four \"enemies\" are practically the same, they just change a little bit in their Paint aspect, but they move slowly towards you and you just have to avoid them. The gifts are all the same sprite, changing just a little bit from city to forest. And there's no purpose in anything, you'll just go on and on endlessly until you'll get hit by a deer or a penguin or whatever it is and you'll instantly re-start with the counter resetted to 0.\nSomething that really has no meaning, if you find this for free or in a bundle.. the only reason you'll want it is maybe for its few achievements, obtainable all in five minutes of play. There are no cards, there's nothing else. So if you're looking for a \"game to play\", just simply run away.",
